                <pb facs="0776" n="676" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg676"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.35E1/68: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-03-10T15:00:00-05:00">March 10, 1934—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>95. For Atherton: Your 108, March 8, noon. Although this Government recognizes
                    the importance of regulating the disposal of surplus crops, it will not be in a
                    position to undertake any commitment regarding them until Congress has acted on
                    the sugar bill now before it.</p>
                <p>Your position with regard to disposal of initial Philippine surplus is
                    approved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
